,title,link,text,language,family
0,Khoe-Kwadi languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khoe–Kwadi_languages,"The Khoe-Kwadi languages are a family consisting of the Khoe languages of southern Africa and the poorly attested extinct Kwadi language of Angola. The relationship has been worked out by Tom Güldemann, Edward Elderkin, and Anne-Maria Fehn.",Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
1,Khoe languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khoe_languages,"The Khoe languages were once considered to be a branch of a Khoisan language family, and were known as Central Khoisan in that scenario. Though Khoisan is now rejected as a family, the name is retained as a term of convenience. The nearest relative of the Khoe family may be the extinct Kwadi language of Angola. This larger group, for which pronouns and some basic vocabulary have been ...",Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
2,Khoe-Kwadi - All Things Linguistic,https://allthingslinguistic.com/post/184998894180/khoe-kwadi,"The most accessible Khoe-Kwadi language is Khoekhoegowab (or ""Standard Namibian Khoekhoe""), one of the major languages of Namibia. There are books and radio programs available in Khoekhoegowab, along with many youtube videos teaching you the sounds and basic sentences.",Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
3,"KHOEKHOE LANGUAGE, PEOPLE, & CULTURE - YouTube",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4-MgRmqIpo4,"""Khoekhoe"" is a term of praise rather than an ethnic name, but it is used to refer to Khoe-speaking pastoralist groups, including the !Ora, !Gona, Nama, Xiri, and ǂNūkhoe.",Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
4,Khoen Collection,http://khoen-collection.org/,"Introduction The present collection provides a digital platform for material and resources available mainly on Khoekhoegowab − but also on its immediate sister languages such as Haiǁ'om and ǂĀkhoe, as well as the, by now extinct Cape Khoekhoe varieties like !Ora (Korana), Xiri (Griqua), and Eini. Khoekhoegowab is a Khoe-Kwadi language subsumed conventionally under the Khoisan languages ...",Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
5,Khoekhoe Media - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCB1V5L9L4sZ4sRTSJc_9k5w/videos,The purpose of the channel is to promote the culture and traditional practices of the Khoekhoe people. Showcase their normal way of doing things and to encourage youngsters to not allow the ...,Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
6,Khoekhoe Translator | Free & AI-Powered - Anything Translate,https://anythingtranslate.com/translators/khoekhoe-translator/,"Description Are you curious about the enchanting Khoekhoe language, a beautiful tongue that resonates the rich heritage of the Khoikhoi people? Look no further than the Khoekhoe Translator! This exceptional online tool effortlessly translates normal language into Khoekhoe, allowing you to explore the vibrant phrases and unique expressions of this indigenous language. With just a few clicks ...",Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
7,PDF Khoekhoegowab tone sandhi and extended projections,https://www.stonybrook.edu/commcms/amp2019/_pdf/_PresentationMaterials/P2-10-Kusmer.pdf,"Tone sandhi Khoekhoegowab (Khoe-Kwadi, Namiba, ~200,000 speakers, also called Khoekhoe) has a process of opaque melodic substitution termed sandhi:",Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
8,"Khoekhoe (Nama) language, alphabet and pronunciation - Omniglot",https://www.omniglot.com/writing/khoekhoe.htm,"Khoekhoe (Khoekhoegowab) Khoekhoe is a Khoe languages spoken mainly in Namibia, and also in South Africa, Botswana and by the Nama (Khoekhoen), Damar and Haiǁom peoples. The language is also known as Nama, and used to be known as Hottentot, although this name is now considered pejorative.",Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
9,Tracing contact and migration in pre-Bantu Southern Africa through ...,https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/evolutionary-human-sciences/article/tracing-contact-and-migration-in-prebantu-southern-africa-through-lexical-borrowing/0E21FE2D0B2AF609FBCC1F4A6F0FE8B5,"Roots that originated in Khoe-Kwadi are most prominent in languages of the Tuu family, whose speakers were in contact with Khoekhoe-speaking herders, suggesting elevated prestige of food producers among resident forager groups. The data further yielded 29% of shared roots for which no origin could be determined.",Khoekhoe,Khoe-Kwadi
